# An or is read as a sum when no bit can be set on both sides, by the
# bits each affine form may set: the low bits a part that is a multiple
# of 2^k leaves to a bounded remainder, and the bits a bounded sum spans.
# Four stores' addresses read so, each with its sectors per warp
# request. A bitwise or that is no sum, and an or with an unbound
# parameter, leave the address unknown; bound to 1, the parameter is
# below 16·%tid.x's lowest bit, and that store reads 64·%tid.x + 4.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/or_disjoint.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN-FREE "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/or_disjoint.ptx --bind 1:n=1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN-BOUND "%s"
ANN-FREE: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r1; // global store [256·%ctaid.x + 4·(⌊%tid.x/8⌋ mod 16) + param_0 + 64] sectors/req 1 (ideal 1){{$}}
ANN-FREE: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r5; // global store [4·(%tid.x mod 16) + 256·uniform(%r3@60) + param_0 + 64] sectors/req 2 (ideal 2){{$}}
ANN-FREE: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r6; // global store [16384·%ctaid.x + 16384·%ctaid.y + 256·(⌊%tid.x/64⌋ mod 2) + param_0 + 512] sectors/req 1 (ideal 1){{$}}
ANN-FREE: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd4], %r2; // global store [64·%ctaid.x + param_0 + 32] sectors/req 1 (ideal 1){{$}}
ANN-FREE: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r2; // global store addr ? (or whose sides may both set bit 4){{$}}
ANN-FREE: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r1; // global store addr ? (or whose sides may both set bit 7){{$}}
ANN-BOUND: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r2; // global store [64·%tid.x + param_0 + 4] sectors/req 32 (ideal 4){{$}}
ANN-BOUND: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r1; // global store addr ? (or whose sides may both set bit 7){{$}}
